"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[1312],{71312:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"rosatom-plavuchie-aes-indoneziya-eksport","locale":"en","title":"Rosatom to make the world\'s first overseas sale of electricity from floating nuclear plants","description":"Rosatom signed the world\'s first export agreement to sell electricity from floating nuclear plants: 2 units totaling 200 MW for Indonesia. What it means for the economy.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 16, 2026, Rosatom and Indonesian company PT Pembangkit Listrik Nuklir signed an agreement at Russian Energy Week to supply eastern Indonesia with electricity. Russia will provide 2 PEB-100 floating nuclear power units, totaling 200 MW, for northern Halmahera island in North Maluku province. Rosatom director Alexei Likhachev called it the world\'s first export agreement to supply electricity from a floating nuclear unit. It is also Indonesia\'s first nuclear project."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"A floating nuclear plant is a small nuclear power station on a barge. It is built at a shipyard and towed to a location lacking transmission networks and space for a large station. Only one currently operates worldwide: the 70 MW Akademik Lomonosov in Chukotka. Kept analyst Sergei Rozhenko says the technology\'s main advantage is speed: capacity becomes available 2–3 times faster than a conventional nuclear station, which takes 8–10 years to build."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"The transaction model matters. Rosatom is selling not merely equipment but electricity throughout the stations\' operating life: 60 years under Rostekhnadzor authorization, with Likhachev expecting an extension. The Indonesian side says the project is commercial, funded privately without Indonesian budget money. First electricity is expected 5 years after the contract\'s principal conditions take effect. Rosatom is also proposing large onshore nuclear plants for Indonesia and holding similar talks in Southeast Asia and Africa."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"The price is undisclosed. A Russian project provides the only reference: in 2021, 4 floating units totaling 420 MW for Chukotka\'s Baimsky mining complex were estimated at 190.2 billion rubles including VAT, with an indicative tariff of about 6 rubles per kWh. The first is due in 2028. Analysts say the economics can be evaluated only after a series of 8–10 units; until then, high initial costs make electricity prices unpredictable."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"Russian export revenue usually follows oil and gas prices. A contract selling electricity for decades earns money independently of oil; more such contracts would reduce the ruble\'s and budget\'s dependence on a single commodity. Floating-unit orders also provide work for Russian shipyards and reactor manufacturers."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"For an ordinary person, the deal changes little in the coming years: electricity will arrive no sooner than 5 years from now, with revenue spread over decades. Its long-term significance concerns the sources of Russia\'s foreign-currency earnings when oil is no longer dominant. Profitability will become clear only when the electricity price and costs are disclosed; neither is public yet."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"What will Rosatom build in Indonesia?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"2 PEB-100 floating nuclear power units totaling 200 MW for northern Halmahera island in North Maluku province. The agreement was signed on October 16, 2026; first electricity is expected 5 years after the principal contract conditions take effect."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What is a floating nuclear plant?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"A small nuclear station on a barge, built at a shipyard and towed to its operating location. The only one currently operating, the 70 MW Akademik Lomonosov, supplies Chukotka."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"How much does a floating nuclear plant cost?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Indonesian project\'s cost is undisclosed. In 2021, 4 floating units for Chukotka were estimated at 190.2 billion rubles including VAT, with an indicated tariff of about 6 rubles per kWh."}],"sources":[{"label":"Nuclear power heads for warmer waters: Rosatom to supply two floating units to Indonesia","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9040651"},{"label":"Rosatom signs agreement for two Indonesian floating nuclear plants","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/business/news/2026/10/16/1237826-rosatom-podpisal-soglashenie"},{"label":"Russia agrees the world\'s first international supply from floating nuclear units","url":"https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/16/rossiya-soglasovala-pervye-v-mire-mezhdunarodnye-postavki-s-plavuchih-atomnyh-energoblokov"}],"sourceBodySha256":"364e6fd7aa47727920a3c88d5445a62573e93f518bfc9c74e7e8f7d9926d5290"}')}}]);